// FittersIQ shared i18n engine -- Stage 0 of the multilingual audit's plan.
// Extracted verbatim from Mobile.html's existing, working I18N/t() system
// (the only real, tested translation infrastructure either app has) so both
// Mobile and Studio can load the SAME dictionary and SAME translation
// helpers from one place, instead of each maintaining its own copy.
//
// Nothing in this file has been changed from what was already live in
// Mobile.html -- same keys, same 10 languages, same localStorage key
// (assembleone_mobile_lang), same behaviour. This stage only moves the
// code; it does not translate anything new, does not touch Studio's
// existing 6-key APP_I18N stub, and does not touch room/customer/job/
// panel data in any way.
//
// Deliberately NOT included here: Mobile's measurement-UNIT picker
// (mm/cm/in -- currentMeasureUnitLabel/paintUnitButton/setMeasureUnitGlobal/
// openUnitPicker) sat physically between openLangPicker() and applyI18n()
// in the original file but is a completely separate feature; it stays
// inline in Mobile.html untouched.
